# Cache Components: time and randomness

This app sets `cacheComponents: true` in `next.config.ts` (Next.js 16). During prerender, **unstable values cannot run in the static shell**.

Forbidden in Server Components / Suspense fallbacks / `loading.js` without a chosen boundary:

- `Date.now()`, `new Date()`, `Date()` (no args)
- `Math.random()`, `crypto.randomUUID()`

Default params are a footgun — `fn(now = Date.now())` still evaluates during prerender.

Canonical error: [blocking-prerender-current-time](https://nextjs.org/docs/messages/blocking-prerender-current-time). Prefer `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` over training data.

## Decision tree (pick one)

| Need | Fix | Pattern in this repo |
|------|-----|----------------------|
| True “now” / relative age (“3 min ago”) on the server | `[dynamic]` `await connection()` then read time; keep the component under a close `<Suspense>` | `components/tfl/week-ahead/week-ahead-section.tsx`, homepage panels in `home-editorial.tsx` |
| Timestamp tied to cached data (“as of” / `fetchedAt`) | `[cache]` call `Date.now()` **inside** the same `"use cache"` function that produces the data; pass the number down; format without a second “now” when possible | `lib/tfl/home-arrivals-data.ts` (`fetchedAt`) |
| Ticking / locale-relative label | `[client]` `"use client"` + set time in `useEffect` / `startTransition` (not during SSR render) | Prefer for live “ago” that updates |
| Timing / telemetry only | `[measure]` `performance.now()` — do not render it | — |

`new Date(knownMs)` / formatting a stored ISO string is fine — the instant is already fixed.

## Do

```tsx
// Request-time "today" or relative age (shell stays static via Suspense)
async function Panel() {
  await connection();
  const label = formatCacheAgeLabel(fetchedAt, Date.now());
  return …;
}
```

```ts
// Stamp when the cache entry was produced — OK inside "use cache"
async function getCached() {
  "use cache";
  cacheLife({ revalidate: 120 });
  return { data, fetchedAt: Date.now() };
}
```

## Don’t

```ts
// ❌ Default arg runs during prerender
export const formatAge = (fetchedAt: number, now = Date.now()) => …;

// ❌ Relative "ago" in a Server Component with no connection() / cache / client
formatAge(payload.fetchedAt);

// ❌ Date.now() in loading.js / Suspense fallback
```

## Related unstable APIs

Same class of fix for `Math.random()` and `crypto.randomUUID()` — cache, defer with `connection()` behind Suspense, or move to the client. See Next.js messages `blocking-prerender-random` and `blocking-prerender-crypto`.
